Free the status bar frame from the menu options

One function serves the frame of a status bar item and the frame of a
popup menu, and one body paints both. The body tests the options of a
popup menu first. A menu background that is not flat, or a popup menu
that is not square, therefore stops the paint of a status bar frame. The
dialog keeps the check box enabled, and its tool tip names status bars
alone, so the option moves no pixel in such a configuration. The frame
also takes the colours of a popup menu, so the shade of the menu
background moves the colour of a status bar.

The status bar arm now stands alone. It tests the option of the status
bar frames, and it takes the colours of the window. The menu arm keeps
every line, so the frame of a popup menu does not move.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 5 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

